  "name": "Visible but Not Avoided: State-Dependent Re-Proposal of Rejected Candidates in Catalog-Based LLM Optimization Loops",
  "notes": "The downstream test uses one screenshot-only agent, nine synthetic apps and 60 cached development items, with TAP-tag or text-answer outputs; this is not demonstrated live-app completion. Two catalogs reword the same 40 edits. Re-proposal effects do not establish internal causal mechanisms or task-success gains. Main serving providers were unpinned; rationale labels came from LLM annotators. No independent reproduction.",
  "published_at": "2026-10-11",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "Studies repeated rejected edits while optimizing a screenshot-only GUI agent, contrasting static probes with reached loop states and testing how rejection wording changes subsequent edit proposals.",
  "topics": [
    "evaluation",
    "grounding",
    "training-free"
  ],
